      expertiseContent:
        'Show how the team tells a pulp enquiry from a paper enquiry, a board enquiry, a converting enquiry, and a print enquiry. That sorting is the useful expertise.\n\nExplain recovered fiber as a route you do or do not quote. Do not attach a percentage you have not published in a grade document.',
      contentFormats:
        'Stage pages, a grade-family index, a form-of-supply note, and a short FAQ fit mills and converters. A retail lookbook of office products does not.\n\nGrade PDFs can support the site when the live page names the same families and does not add speeds or percentages the PDF does not contain.',
      buyerJourney:
        'A buyer identifies the stage, checks form and family, and sends quantity and document needs. Clarification and a quote follow.\n\nA trial reel or a converting trial may come later. The form is not an order and it is not a print job.',
      salesCycleCharacteristics:
        'Quotes wait on stage, family, form, and quantity. Converting quotes also wait on the finished format. Revision is normal when the downstream line changes.\n\nSay who answers and which missing fact pauses the quote. Do not promise a ship date the mill has not confirmed.',
