        'Organize by pulp, paper, board, and converting. Put printing in its own section if you print, and keep it labeled as printing. Keep any office channel off the mill navigation.\n\nThe enquiry should capture stage, family, form, and quantity, plus a file upload when a specification exists.',
      paidAdvertisingStrategy:
        'Send pulp queries to the pulp page, board queries to the board page, and converting queries to the converter page. Sending all of them to a homepage headline wastes the click.\n\nNegative keywords for copy shops, office retail, and student printing reduce spend if you do not sell those services.',
      conversionOptimization:
        'Ask for stage, grade family, form, quantity, and documents. Say what happens next. Remove fields that demand a machine speed or a recycled-content percentage you will not publish.\n\nIf converting needs a finished-format note, show that field only after the visitor chooses converting.',
      analyticsAndMeasurement:
        'Count enquiries that name a stage and a form. Split pulp, paper, board, and converting. Do not report those enquiries as tons or as revenue.\n\nWatch how often print and office queries land here. A high share means the page is still attracting the wrong intent.',
