      targetMarkets:
        'Customers are usually OEMs and tier suppliers buying parts, product companies buying compound, and maintenance buyers at plants replacing industrial rubber parts in production quantities. A consumer shop selling a single mat is not the audience.\n\nGeography matters for compound supply, tooling, and bonded-part logistics. Say which you support.',
      buyerTypes:
        'Materials engineers check the compound route. Design engineers check molding or extrusion feasibility. Procurement checks tooling, quantity, and documents. A maintenance buyer with a one-off consumer request is a different, usually unwanted, path.\n\nA site that only shows black parts on a white background, with no process label, loses the engineer who must choose compound versus part.',
