        'Engineering accepts the process and the family. Procurement accepts commercial terms and tooling ownership. Quality may ask which records you will discuss. Do not answer that question with an unearned certificate.\n\nWhen a bonded insert changes the supplier set, say who machines or stamps the insert and who bonds it.',
      buyerRequirements:
        'A compound enquiry names the family, the supply form, and the quantity. A molding or extrusion enquiry names the process, the part or profile, the quantity, and whether tooling exists. A finished-part enquiry adds assembly steps and any insert or reinforcement.\n\nThe form should ask which of the four steps the visitor wants. A drawing with no process is a weak start.',
      purchasingFactors:
        'Selection turns on process fit, elastomer family, tooling responsibility, documents, and lead time. A slogan about advanced elastomers does not replace that list.\n\nBuyers also compare a compounder who sells stock with a molder who buys stock and sells parts. Label the role.',
